finding: P2 — The complete-state inventory excludes a cache that upstream still reads for shapes explicitly in scope. README.md:54 says omitting convex caches is exact for box-against-round shapes, but at 3362633 src/contact.c:488,521-527 passes contact->convexContact.cache.simplexCache to both b3CollideHullAndSphere and b3CollideHullAndCapsule. src/convex_manifold.c:664 consumes it through b3ShapeDistance, and src/distance.c:731-755 reads its count, indices and metric. adapter/step.c recreates each contact and never loads this state; SetContactRecycleDistance(0) disables relative-pose contact recycling, not the GJK simplex cache. Consequently uninterrupted rollout retains and updates this state while every loaded step starts it empty. The 240-step fixture and sentinel both pass without testing or disabling this field, so they do not establish the claimed inventory completeness. Carry it, or actually disable/refuse this path with an explicit supported-scene restriction and evidence; do not claim box-round is cache-free. Independent checks: bun test test/step.test.ts passed (2 tests, 248 assertions). The GPU cartpole test independently passed all 600 steps in four worlds on M4 Max, with the reported maxima reproduced. No expected ragdoll continuous red counted. Narrow additional probe: stepping each native ragdoll pre-state independently against its uninterrupted next result (180 steps) is not bit-equal; maximum normalized continuous discrepancy was 9.423494338989258e-5 at step 80, body 2 angular velocity x, with no discrete mismatch. That probe alone does not localize the discrepancy to the omitted cache and is not a separate finding.
